## What changed

**`src/retry.ts`** — implemented `retry`:
- Validates `attempts` up front and throws a `RangeError` before `fn` ever runs.
- Calls `fn` up to `attempts` times, returning its first result.
- After failure `n` (when more attempts remain), awaits `sleep(baseMs * 2 ** (n - 1))` — so `baseMs`, `2·baseMs`, `4·baseMs`… No sleep after the final failure.
- On exhaustion throws `new Error(\`gave up after ${attempts} attempts: ${message}\`, { cause: lastError })`.
- `sleep` defaults to a real `setTimeout` wait.

**`src/retry.test.ts`** (new) — 6 tests with a fake sleep that records every `ms` it was asked to wait: first-try success (and that `sleep` was never called), success on the last attempt, exact wait sequence `[baseMs, 2·baseMs, 4·baseMs]`, give-up (call count, message, `cause` identity, wait sequence), `RangeError` for `attempts` 0/-1/-42 (asserting `fn` never ran), and the default-sleep path timed with real `setTimeout`.

