## Decisions the plan didn't specify

- **Non-integer `attempts` also throws `RangeError`** (e.g. `2.5`) — a fractional attempt count makes the backoff sequence meaningless; this only extends the "below 1" rule, never weakens it.
- **Give-up message uses the last error's `.message` when it's an `Error`**, else `String(lastError)` — so the message reads `gave up after 4 attempts: disk on fire`, not `…: Error: disk on fire`, which `String(error)` would have produced.
- One test of mine initially failed (I forgot to catch the expected rejection in the default-sleep timing test); fixed the test, not the implementation.

Caveat: `tsc` can't typecheck the test file because `bun-types` isn't installed in this workspace (only `bun test` exists as a toolchain), so the tests are verified by execution only.

